<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Council of Portugal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1582">1582</a>–<a href="/years/1668">1668</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Council of Portugal was the royal council created by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-spain">Philip II of Spain</a> in 1582 to advise the king on Portuguese affairs during the union of the crowns. Sitting at the court in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrid">Madrid</a> and staffed by Portuguese, it handled appointments, petitions and government business for Portugal and its empire. It lost its purpose with the Portuguese Restoration of 1640.</p></div>
